      "at": "2026-09-25T15:54:07Z",
      "excerpt": "CodSpeed on 78be756 flags two regressions: - `test_state_access[write_own]` (-7%) is the per-write lock check (`_check_writable`) that this PR adds. It is the expected cost, as noted earlier. - `test_get_state_uncached[memory]` (-7%) is not caused by this PR, as far as I can tell. Building a fresh tree runs the same number of Python calls on stage 1 (227738e) and on this head: 15002 for 300 trees, under cProfile. The only addition on that path is one slot store per state (`_event_context = None`"
