      "at": "2026-09-25T19:20:32Z",
      "excerpt": "CodSpeed on 0e2624a confirms the fix: `test_get_state_uncached[memory]` and `test_state_manager_memory_cold_get` are no longer flagged. Two regressions remain, and both are the per-write lock check (`_check_writable`) that this PR adds: - `test_state_access[write_own]` (-11%) measures exactly those writes. - `test_set_state[memory]` (-5%) dirties the tree with two field writes (`_touch`) before each `set_state`. The memory manager's `set_state` does almost nothing else, so the two checks make up"
